**About MAF = 0.8:** Minor Allele Frequency (MAF) is defined as the frequency of the *less common* allele, so by definition MAF ≤ 0.5. A threshold of 0.8 would filter out **every single SNP** — no variant can have MAF > 0.8. Did you perhaps mean:

- **MAF = 0.08** (filter out rare variants below 8%)?
- **MAF = 0.01** (standard GWAS threshold)?
- Or something else entirely (e.g., a genotyping rate / call rate threshold of 0.8)?

