     ## MAF = 0.8 — Fatal Problem                                               
                                                                                
     MAF (Minor Allele Frequency) is the frequency of the **less common**       
     allele, so by definition **MAF ≤ 0.5** for every SNP in the genome. A      
     threshold of **0.8** would filter out **100% of all SNPs**, leaving        
     you with zero variants and no GWAS results.                                
                                                                                
     **Did you mean one of these?**                                             
                                                                                
     - **MAF = 0.08** — keep SNPs with minor allele frequency ≥ 8%              
     - **MAF = 0.01** — standard GWAS threshold (keep common variants ≥ 1%)     
     - **MAF = 0.05** — default in piggpa-G (keep variants ≥ 5%)                
     - **Genotyping rate / call rate = 0.8** — keep SNPs genotyped in ≥ 80%     
     of samples                                                                 
     - Something else?                                                          
                                                                                
